# Test: offline decode of an OSPFv2 packet with a non-zero Instance ID (spec-ospf-ext-12).
#
# VALIDATES: `ze ospf decode` renders the RFC 6549 Instance ID (header offset 14) and the
# 8-bit AuType (offset 15) as SEPARATE JSON fields. The input is a 44-octet OSPFv2 Hello
# with Instance ID 5 (byte 14 = 0x05) and AuType 0 (byte 15 = 0x00).
# PREVENTS: a regression where the decoder folds the two octets back into a single 16-bit
# AuType, or drops the Instance ID from the decoded view.

# Hex OSPFv2 Hello: header (24) + Hello body (20). Byte 14 = 05 (Instance ID),
# byte 15 = 00 (AuType), router-id 10.0.0.1, area 0.0.0.0, length 0x002c = 44.
stdin=ospf-hello-hex:terminator=EOF_HEX
0201002c0a00000100000000000005000000000000000000ffffff00000a0201000000280000000000000000
EOF_HEX

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze ospf decode:stdin=ospf-hello-hex
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains="type":"hello"
expect=stdout:contains="instance-id":5
expect=stdout:contains="auth-type":0
